			"notes": "# 📦 ChestLogger v2.7.0\n\n> **Multi-Version Release Matrix (Minecraft 26.2 & 26.3), Double Chest Logging Overhaul & Client GUI Enhancements**\n\n---\n\n### 🌟 Highlights & Summary\n\nChestLogger **v2.7.0** introduces our new **Multi-Version Release Matrix**, providing simultaneous first-class support for both **Minecraft 26.3** and **Minecraft 26.2** across Fabric and Paper. This release resolves transaction duplication on 54-slot double chests, introduces unified log merging across single/double chest state changes, and fixes search bar keyboard input on Fabric client GUIs.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Major Upgrades\n\n#### 1. Multi-Version Release Matrix (SemVer 2.0 Build Metadata)\nAll release artifacts now follow SemVer 2.0 build metadata (`<mod_version>+<mc_version>`), ensuring older long-term server versions (26.2) receive identical bug fixes, security updates, and performance patches alongside new adoption targets (26.3):\n\n| Platform | Target Version | Artifact Name | Compatibility |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Fabric** | **Minecraft 26.3** | `chestlogger-fabric-2.7.0+26.3.jar` | Fabric Loader $\\ge 0.19.5$, Fabric API `0.161.0+26.3` |\n| **Fabric** | **Minecraft 26.2** | `chestlogger-fabric-2.7.0+26.2.jar` | Fabric Loader $\\ge 0.19.3$, Fabric API `0.157.0+26.2` |\n| **Paper** | **Minecraft 26.3** | `chestlogger-paper-2.7.0+26.3.jar` | Paper 26.3 builds, Java 25 |\n| **Paper** | **Minecraft 26.2** | `chestlogger-paper-2.7.0+26.2.jar` | Paper 26.2 builds, Java 25 |\n\n#### 2. Native Minecraft 26.3 Support\n* Full ecosystem alignment with Minecraft 26.3 on Fabric and Paper.\n* Modernized client input backend and updated toolchains.\n\n---\n\n### 🐛 Bug Fixes & Engine Improvements\n\n#### 1. Double Chest Transaction Deduplication\n* **Issue:** Placing or withdrawing items from a double chest previously caused duplicate transaction records to be generated across both container block entities.\n* **Fix:** Implemented coordinate half-partitioning across both Fabric mixins (`AbstractContainerMenuMixin`, `HopperBlockEntityMixin`, `ContainerTracker`) and Paper listeners (`PaperChestEventListener`). Slots `0–26` are assigned strictly to the primary chest block coordinate, while slots `27–53` are assigned to the secondary partner coordinate, guaranteeing zero duplication.\n\n#### 2. Unified Historical Log Merging for Double Chests\n* **Issue:** When a double chest was created or converted, older transaction history was trapped on the original half, causing inspection tools to only show partial history depending on which half was clicked.\n* **Fix:** Inspection tools (Inspection Wand, `/chestlog inspect`, and GUI viewer) now dynamically detect double chest partners and query the unified transaction log for both coordinates simultaneously. Transitioning between single and double chests preserves the complete historical timeline.\n\n#### 3. Fabric Client GUI Search Input Restored\n* **Issue:** Players were unable to focus or type text into the filter search box in `ChestLogScreen` and `ChestLogFilterWidget` under Minecraft 26.3.\n* **Fix:** Updated event propagation, focus management, and key-press handling to conform to the 26.3 client input pipeline.\n\n---\n\n### ⚠️ Things to Consider / Upgrade Guide\n\n1. **Java Runtime Requirement:**\n   * Both **Minecraft 26.2** and **Minecraft 26.3** run on **Java 25**. Ensure your server startup scripts use Java 25 JRE/JDK.\n2. **Zero Database Migration Needed:**\n   * Storage format (append-only binary logs and `.idx` persistent checkpoints) is 100% backward-compatible with `v2.6.x` data. You can perform an in-place upgrade without wiping logs or rebuilding indexes.\n3. **Choosing Your JAR:**\n   * **Fabric Users/Admins:** Download the JAR matching your client/server Minecraft version (`+26.3` or `+26.2`).\n   * **Paper Server Admins:** Download the JAR matching your Paper server branch (`+26.3` or `+26.2`).\n\n---\n\n### 📥 Download Binaries\n\n..."
		},
